# Map: Internal tool — stack, skeleton, conventions

## Destination

A decided frontend stack, a scaffolded skeleton on disk, and the project's
conventions locked — the point at which the first feature slices can be handed
to `/espalier`. Shipping features and deploying are past this destination.

## Notes

- Domain: internal tooling; single team, no external users assumed.
- Stack is OPEN. The originating request named `npx create-next-app@latest`,
  but the team has more Svelte experience, so Next.js is a default reach and
  not a decision. Nothing in this map may assume Next.js until ticket 002 closes.
- No scaffold command runs outside a task ticket's user-approved write window
  (see ticket 003). Charting writes nothing outside `espalier/maps/`.
- `espalier/rules/` and `espalier/wiki/` are empty, so the grill's convention
  cross-check has nothing to check against. After the skeleton exists,
  `/espalier-init` is the natural way to encode the conventions this map decides.
- Open Question (asked, unanswered this session): what the tool's core job is
  and who the first user is. Conservative default until answered — the
  destination stays bounded to skeleton + conventions, and no feature scope
  enters this map. Charted as ticket 001 so it gets answered rather than assumed.

## Decisions so far

<!-- the index — one line per closed ticket; the detail lives in the ticket -->

## Not yet specified

- How users authenticate and who is allowed in (company SSO vs. something simpler).
- Whether the tool owns data or only reads existing systems, and what persists it.
- Where it runs and who deploys it.
- Whether other internal systems need to call it, i.e. whether it needs an API
  surface at all.

## Out of scope

- Building any feature of the tool — that is `/espalier` work past this map's handoff.
- Deployment and hosting setup — past the destination.

