claimed_at:
---

## Question

Nothing to decide here — this is the manual work that unblocks the convention
decisions in ticket 004. The conventions question ("what do we still have to
choose once the framework's defaults are in place?") cannot be answered against
an imagined skeleton, only against a real one.

Run the CLI for whichever framework ticket 002 selects — `create-next-app` or
`sv create` — with the options that ticket's resolution names, and record in
the Resolution what the scaffold actually put on disk: directory layout, test
runner, linter/formatter, TypeScript settings, routing style.

This ticket writes outside `espalier/maps/`, which the session marker's guard
blocks by default. Protocol when working it:

1. Ask the user first (run it / hand them a checklist / skip).
2. On approval, append an `allow:` line per approved path prefix to
   `espalier/maps/.active-session`.
3. Run the scaffold.
4. The window dies with the marker at session end — it is not a standing grant.

Do not run this before ticket 002 closes. Scaffolding first would lock the
framework choice as a filesystem fact and reduce ticket 002 to a rubber stamp.

## Resolution
```

